course: dictionary
lesson: 5561
title: What a lens does
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lens is a curved piece of glass or plastic that bends light. Because it bends light, things can look bigger, smaller or clearer. «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» The word bent is your clue: the lens changes the path of the light.
explain: Lenses are in many places: glasses, cameras, microscopes and telescopes. Your own eye has a lens too. The lens of the eye is the clear part behind the pupil, and it focuses light. «The lens in the eye works like a magnifying glass and makes an upside-down picture on the retina at the back of the eye.»
explain: Read the words around lens to see which kind it is. «A contact lens» is a thin lens you wear on your eye, so a lens can be very small. «A camera lens» needs to be clean. Ask yourself: does "a curved piece that bends light" fit this sentence? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A lens is a curved piece of glass or plastic that bends light.
fact: A magnifying glass uses a convex lens to make things look bigger.
fact: «A cataract is when the lens inside the eye becomes cloudy, usually with age.»
fact: Glasses bend light a little more or less, so the picture lands right on the retina.
fact: Never point a lens at the Sun: it can gather sunlight into a tiny burning spot.
exercise: «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» What is the lens doing to the light? | It makes the light colder | *It bends the light | It turns the light into sound | It stops the light completely
exercise: A contact lens is worn where? | On your teeth | Under your hat | In your pocket | *On your eye
exercise: Which of these uses a lens? | A cup of tea | *A microscope | A wooden spoon | A bicycle bell
test: «The lens in the eye works like a magnifying glass.» What does the lens of the eye do? | It keeps your body warm | It stores food | It makes sound | *It focuses light
test: What is a cataract? | A cold that spreads from person to person | *A cloudy lens inside the eye | A sore on the skin | A kind of camera
exam: Which word means the clear part behind the pupil that focuses light? | Pupil | Iris | Retina | *Lens
